WEBVTT

00:58.475 --> 01:00.143
Atmospheric instability

01:00.226 --> 01:03.563
is the collision of two types of air
with different properties.

02:02.914 --> 02:03.790
I'm late.

02:20.056 --> 02:21.099
I'm not ready yet.

02:21.599 --> 02:23.685
- Oh, no, we can't go in together.
- We're gonna be late, though.

02:23.768 --> 02:25.145
Not "we," just you.

02:33.069 --> 02:34.404
THE EFFECTIVENESS OF FOG ADVISORIES
AND CASES FROM ABROAD

02:57.927 --> 02:58.887
Hello?

03:26.539 --> 03:27.916
So what do you want me to do?

03:28.958 --> 03:31.628
Listen. I won't do anything for you.

03:31.711 --> 03:33.588
Not anymore. And I can't anyway!

03:34.380 --> 03:35.673
And don't ever call me.

03:48.228 --> 03:52.732
When cold air
suddenly meets hot air…

03:56.444 --> 03:58.112
I, uh, forgot my hard drive.

03:59.239 --> 04:00.156
Ah.

04:02.825 --> 04:04.202
I was gonna bring it for you.

04:07.914 --> 04:08.748
Well, thanks.

04:11.167 --> 04:13.169
So, um, who was that?

04:17.215 --> 04:19.008
It's just someone that I used to know.

04:20.301 --> 04:21.177
Oh.

04:22.845 --> 04:26.766
…the atmosphere becomes unstable
and severe weather occurs.

04:29.060 --> 04:31.354
Shouldn't you go? You're gonna be late.

04:31.938 --> 04:33.439
Uh, yeah, I should.

04:36.985 --> 04:38.319
Uh, I'll go along.

04:42.782 --> 04:44.909
Where are you going?
We need to talk.

04:44.993 --> 04:45.910
Later.

04:51.457 --> 04:53.418
I didn't know you were someone
who holds a grudge.

04:54.002 --> 04:56.379
What?

04:56.462 --> 04:58.214
Do you think I'm holding
a grudge right now?

04:58.298 --> 05:00.258
Okay, so Lee Si-woo
and I went on some dates.

05:00.341 --> 05:02.844
I met him when I was working
at the Metro Office.

05:02.927 --> 05:04.595
He was nice,
and for a few months, we went out.

05:05.179 --> 05:06.931
So? Anything else you want to know?

05:07.515 --> 05:10.476
How about my college crushes,
my first love in high school?

05:10.560 --> 05:12.603
Why can't you see why I'm upset?

05:12.687 --> 05:15.356
You think this is just about a guy
you happened to date?

05:15.440 --> 05:16.441
Oh, it's not?

05:16.524 --> 05:17.775
You lied to me before.

05:17.859 --> 05:19.569
You said you never met him.

05:19.652 --> 05:21.279
I just don't get why you would lie.

05:21.863 --> 05:24.949
I didn't want things to be uncomfortable
since we all work together.

05:26.075 --> 05:27.744
Just like how uncomfortable I am

05:27.827 --> 05:29.829
seeing that woman
every time I go in there.

05:29.912 --> 05:32.582
I'm not okay with it
just because I don't say anything.

05:33.166 --> 05:35.668
I told you about her at the start.
I told you if I had--

05:35.752 --> 05:38.463
And you have always told me
that the past is the past, so…

05:40.423 --> 05:41.299
Ah.

05:42.467 --> 05:44.510
So you're saying
it was the past at our wedding

05:44.594 --> 05:46.304
when he made a whole scene over us?

05:49.599 --> 05:51.476
Forget it.

05:54.937 --> 05:56.439
Hey, we're not done talking.

05:57.023 --> 05:59.233
I'll be late if I stay here any longer.

05:59.317 --> 06:01.361
Plus, I have to clean up
your whole mess too.

06:23.508 --> 06:26.761
Warmer weather right now
than we usually see in early June.

06:26.844 --> 06:30.139
Today will be a hot one
with temperatures rising sharply.

06:30.223 --> 06:34.060
Currently, 23 degrees in Seoul
and 21 in Incheon,

06:34.143 --> 06:36.229
down one or two degrees from yesterday.

06:36.312 --> 06:39.816
But midday temperatures
are expected to get as high as 29 degrees.

06:39.899 --> 06:41.859
Even though June is the start of summer,

06:41.943 --> 06:44.278
we won't see true summer heat
for a little while.

06:44.362 --> 06:46.406
Skies are looking clear all day.

06:46.489 --> 06:48.783
Cloudless skies mean strong
direct sun throughout the day,

06:48.866 --> 06:50.451
so be mindful of UV…

06:50.535 --> 06:52.703
You should drive with both your hands
on the wheel.

06:52.787 --> 06:55.123
I'm good with just one, though.

06:56.457 --> 06:58.376
Drive safely, though.

06:59.919 --> 07:00.962
Okay.

07:02.713 --> 07:04.590
Two different mindsets.

07:08.219 --> 07:09.887
CHAE YU-JIN

07:15.184 --> 07:16.018
Um…

07:16.102 --> 07:17.937
I have to drive safely right now.

07:18.521 --> 07:19.439
Right?

07:22.191 --> 07:24.068
Two different scars.

07:29.657 --> 07:34.704
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

07:38.833 --> 07:40.418
Drop me off in front of the crosswalk.

07:41.043 --> 07:42.378
Why? We're almost there.

07:42.462 --> 07:43.713
Why can't we just go?

07:43.796 --> 07:44.964
Drop me off.

07:45.047 --> 07:46.924
Jeez, just 'cause somebody could see us?

07:47.008 --> 07:48.843
I could just say I ran into you
coming over here.

07:48.926 --> 07:50.386
Should I just get out?

07:51.762 --> 07:55.475
Just like when cold air
suddenly meets hot air,

07:55.558 --> 07:59.353
you and I, two different people, met.

08:02.982 --> 08:03.900
All right.

08:04.525 --> 08:06.444
I'll drop you off over there.

08:06.527 --> 08:08.362
You should get over right now.

08:12.325 --> 08:13.284
Mm?

08:15.203 --> 08:16.454
Uh…

08:26.422 --> 08:28.257
We already committed to this.

08:29.634 --> 08:32.887
How much unstable climates
caused by this decision

08:33.596 --> 08:35.515
will we be able to avoid?

08:36.807 --> 08:43.064
EPISODE 5
LOCALIZED HEAVY RAIN

08:49.320 --> 08:50.655
Say something.

08:55.117 --> 08:57.078
- We met on our way here.
- Huh?

08:58.079 --> 09:00.831
It's just we, by total coincidence,
ran into each other.

09:01.791 --> 09:02.708
Uh-huh.

09:03.709 --> 09:04.961
What a coincidence.

09:11.342 --> 09:13.886
Looks like traffic in Uijeongbu
has been backed up all morning

09:13.970 --> 09:15.304
'cause the roads are flooded.

09:15.388 --> 09:16.764
The Jungnang River overflowed.

09:17.473 --> 09:19.308
"Flooded"? The Jungnang River?

09:19.892 --> 09:21.852
It rained in Uijeongbu overnight.

09:21.936 --> 09:23.479
It was like 50mm per hour.

09:23.563 --> 09:24.814
Rain?

09:27.775 --> 09:28.943
Mm.

09:29.777 --> 09:32.196
Uh, I'm not, uh…

09:33.030 --> 09:35.324
Isn't it too early
for localized heavy rainfall like this?

09:35.408 --> 09:39.078
In terms of development,
it's a pretty standard sudden downpour.

09:39.161 --> 09:40.913
It took exactly 21 minutes

09:40.997 --> 09:44.625
for Uijeongbu's rain
to travel to Namyangju.

09:44.709 --> 09:47.253
A heavy rain advisory
was issued around 5:30 a.m.

09:47.336 --> 09:50.298
Total predicted rainfall
is somewhere around 70 and 80mm.

09:50.381 --> 09:52.717
Where's
the precipitation concentrated?

09:52.800 --> 09:54.635
Near the Jungnang River footbridge.

09:54.719 --> 09:56.596
Jungnang River? My goodness.

09:56.679 --> 09:59.682
And I guess by the time the advisory
was out, it was already too late.

10:00.266 --> 10:01.851
- Yes.
- Oh!

10:02.727 --> 10:05.354
Director Jin. What do you think?

10:05.438 --> 10:08.441
Don't you think
the water vapor inflow is oddly high?

10:08.524 --> 10:11.027
Yesterday's daytime high
was around 30 degrees

10:11.110 --> 10:13.613
and provided a lot of ground heat
in that region.

10:13.696 --> 10:17.950
As a result, the atmosphere over there
is likely to create strong conditions.

10:18.034 --> 10:21.037
No, no, the biggest cause
looks like the instability

10:21.120 --> 10:22.663
just north of Uijeongbu.

10:22.747 --> 10:24.749
The air's, the air's extremely cold.

10:24.832 --> 10:27.084
Huh? Elaborate.

10:27.710 --> 10:30.171
Oh! So, if you look over here,
the temperature difference

10:30.254 --> 10:32.256
between the upper and lower layers
of the atmosphere

10:32.340 --> 10:34.342
near Uijeongbu is almost 40 degrees.

10:37.803 --> 10:38.679
Mm.

10:39.305 --> 10:40.306
- Director Jin.
- Yes?

10:40.890 --> 10:43.476
- Run an analysis for this.
- Yes, of course.

10:45.936 --> 10:48.314
How astute. Well done.

10:48.814 --> 10:50.191
I'm glad I brought you here
to Headquarters.

10:50.274 --> 10:52.109
Thank you, sir.

10:53.194 --> 10:55.738
All right, then.

10:59.700 --> 11:01.661
Of all those rain echoes,

11:01.744 --> 11:04.705
how do you know which one
will develop into a sudden storm?

11:04.789 --> 11:05.956
With only an hour?

11:07.083 --> 11:09.293
Let's say you started boiling water
on a stove.

11:09.877 --> 11:11.796
It's similar to guessing
the place in the pot

11:11.879 --> 11:14.090
where the bubbles
are going to start first.

11:14.173 --> 11:15.216
Huh?

11:16.550 --> 11:20.388
It's better not to try and predict
if you're trying not to go crazy.

11:23.891 --> 11:25.434
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

11:25.518 --> 11:27.561
All right, all right.

11:27.645 --> 11:29.271
Don't worry, huh?

11:29.855 --> 11:31.190
Think of it like a quick jab

11:31.273 --> 11:33.192
thrown from the sky
to keep us on our toes.

11:33.275 --> 11:34.193
All right?

11:34.902 --> 11:37.697
So let's all stay responsible, eyes open.

11:37.780 --> 11:38.698
Okay?

11:40.241 --> 11:42.660
Quick reporting of storms is vital.

11:43.577 --> 11:44.453
That is all.

11:44.537 --> 11:45.621
Good job, everyone.

11:45.705 --> 11:47.206
- Thank you, sir.
- Thank you.

11:47.289 --> 11:48.207
Thank you, sir.

11:48.290 --> 11:49.208
Thank you.

11:50.960 --> 11:52.586
- How you doing?
- What's up, man?

11:53.379 --> 11:55.047
I'm sorry, ma'am. I'm sorry I'm late.

11:56.966 --> 11:58.801
- Mr. Um.
- Yes?

12:02.805 --> 12:03.889
Let's talk over coffee.

12:05.224 --> 12:07.435
Come on.

12:07.518 --> 12:08.436
Yes, sir.

12:20.573 --> 12:23.576
Oh. Mm… Thanks.

12:24.744 --> 12:27.496
Didn't you go straight home
after we got that drink last night?

12:27.580 --> 12:32.001
Ah! I couldn't sleep,
so I thought I'd have one more, eh.

12:32.084 --> 12:34.795
- And one led to--
- Well, this is a new one.

12:34.879 --> 12:36.338
The great Um Dong-han

12:36.422 --> 12:39.508
showing up during monsoon season late
and with a hangover.

12:42.928 --> 12:45.181
So what's going on?

12:46.390 --> 12:49.977
The sky changes, it's…
It's a new pattern every three days.

12:50.060 --> 12:52.104
Again, always stay the same.

12:53.731 --> 12:55.107
Something wrong at the house?

12:57.485 --> 12:58.736
No, nothing's wrong.

13:04.617 --> 13:06.202
All you care about is weather.

13:06.786 --> 13:09.038
Any kind of weather,
you'll go sun, you'll go storms.

13:09.121 --> 13:12.917
You'll wander around the whole world
and maybe stop at home for a day.

13:13.000 --> 13:14.502
Then the next morning, you tell me

13:14.585 --> 13:16.879
you would have to leave again
for some stupid reason, right?

13:16.962 --> 13:18.756
You were never there, ever.

13:19.340 --> 13:21.050
So we've tried to move on.

13:22.218 --> 13:23.969
We've made it 14 years without you.

13:24.762 --> 13:26.180
You understand me now?

13:54.166 --> 13:56.710
What's this? Going somewhere?

13:59.129 --> 14:00.297
Oh, um…

14:01.257 --> 14:03.175
I must stay at the office for a while.

14:04.593 --> 14:07.304
There's a lot of work to do
during the monsoon season.

14:08.389 --> 14:09.807
Do you really have to go?

14:10.474 --> 14:12.643
This way, everything's easier
for you and Bo-mi.

14:12.726 --> 14:13.978
Do what you want.

14:14.520 --> 14:16.564
If you're gonna be like this,
you should have stayed away.

14:59.315 --> 15:01.609
Does Senior Forecaster Um
drink a lot?

15:01.692 --> 15:04.612
- I don't know. Not that I've heard of.
- Hmm.

15:05.195 --> 15:08.824
Well, I guess it must be hard for him
'cause of his failed promotion.

15:08.908 --> 15:10.451
Don't you think? Hmm?

15:11.452 --> 15:12.328
Well, I think so.

15:13.203 --> 15:14.163
I don't know.

15:14.246 --> 15:15.915
Hello. Attention, everyone.

15:16.957 --> 15:17.958
We're going to analyze

15:18.042 --> 15:20.502
the flash flood-related signals
over the past ten years,

15:20.586 --> 15:23.631
including duration and levels
as well as sort it by region.

15:23.714 --> 15:24.882
Everything for ten years?

15:24.965 --> 15:25.883
Yes.

15:27.676 --> 15:29.970
Is ten years of reports really necessary?

15:30.554 --> 15:32.723
This morning was
an extremely unusual case.

15:32.806 --> 15:34.391
It was, but climate change

15:34.475 --> 15:37.269
could still be increasing
the overall likelihood of such phenomena.

15:37.353 --> 15:39.521
We need to think long-term about it, okay?

15:39.605 --> 15:41.357
There's a lot of uncertainty right now.

15:41.440 --> 15:44.652
I think a short-term analysis
would be more helpful

15:44.735 --> 15:47.071
in supporting our forecasting goals
at the current moment.

15:47.154 --> 15:50.115
The Director General also said
real-time monitoring is key.

15:50.199 --> 15:53.619
Isn't real-time monitoring
more valuable in this situation?

16:06.840 --> 16:09.385
Let's proceed with our ten years
of analysis, please.

16:12.596 --> 16:15.766
Ugh, today really sucks.

16:43.335 --> 16:44.503
HOW ACCURATE IS THE RAIN FORECAST?

16:44.586 --> 16:46.797
- Did you check?
- I'll call them right now.

16:48.007 --> 16:49.049
What is this?

16:49.550 --> 16:51.510
Why are the article stories all different?

16:51.593 --> 16:54.471
We found out about the flood
after the advisory was issued.

16:54.555 --> 16:57.808
We put out the press release right away.
But some outlets had already printed.

17:01.729 --> 17:04.940
- Which team is in charge right now?
- They probably changed shifts already.

17:05.941 --> 17:06.984
So it's Two right now.

17:07.067 --> 17:08.694
Our second team?

17:12.740 --> 17:15.325
TREAT THE SKIES AS A FRIEND
AND THE PEOPLE AS THE SKIES

17:15.409 --> 17:17.327
"Chief Team Two."

17:18.996 --> 17:21.248
Chief Team Two. Chief Team Two.

17:24.585 --> 17:27.463
Chief Team Two. Chief Team Two.

17:31.508 --> 17:33.010
FORECAST TRAINING

17:43.062 --> 17:43.896
I got a call

17:44.688 --> 17:45.564
What call?

17:54.823 --> 17:57.910
We're over now. How long
will I keep getting these calls?

17:57.993 --> 17:58.952
I'm sorry.

18:00.162 --> 18:01.538
You can block the number.

18:01.622 --> 18:03.957
I'm already in enough trouble
right now because of you.

18:04.041 --> 18:05.250
Because of me?

18:05.334 --> 18:06.668
Ki-jun found out the truth.

18:07.586 --> 18:08.837
He found out about us two.

18:08.921 --> 18:10.839
It's already done, so what's the problem?

18:12.382 --> 18:14.676
Why did you have to make a scene
at my wedding, though?

18:14.760 --> 18:18.847
Also, why did you have to transfer
to Headquarters right after my honeymoon?

18:19.932 --> 18:22.476
I can't blame Ki-jun
for thinking this is all strange.

18:26.605 --> 18:27.564
So?

18:28.732 --> 18:29.775
You two fought?

18:31.693 --> 18:33.112
And now he's mad, huh?

18:35.447 --> 18:37.407
Ki-jun is not that kind of person.

18:38.033 --> 18:39.201
He's really in love with me.

18:40.077 --> 18:42.621
He wouldn't get bitter
over something that doesn't matter.

18:44.206 --> 18:46.917
Okay. Well, I guess I'll be more careful.
That all you want?

18:47.000 --> 18:48.335
Of course. Of course, that's all.

18:52.047 --> 18:53.382
Uh, oppa.

19:05.811 --> 19:06.979
What are you doing?

19:07.771 --> 19:08.814
We were just talking.

19:09.481 --> 19:10.524
You know…

19:11.733 --> 19:14.403
the Weather Team shouldn't ever talk
directly to the media.

19:15.362 --> 19:17.614
That's what
the Spokesperson's Office is for.

19:19.074 --> 19:23.328
This is why every newspaper in town
has different stories about the rain.

19:23.412 --> 19:25.914
Can I talk to you, oppa?
I can explain this.

19:25.998 --> 19:28.125
Stay out of this, reporter.
This is KMA business.

19:29.793 --> 19:31.837
Why are you like this, huh?

19:31.920 --> 19:34.339
I guess I don't know
'cause you just started at Headquarters.

19:34.423 --> 19:36.258
The Spokesperson's Office
is the voice of KMA.

19:36.341 --> 19:39.261
Even if your forecast is good,
if you don't work with the Spokesperson,

19:39.344 --> 19:41.096
the reports are going to be
all over the place

19:41.180 --> 19:42.472
like the flash flood release this morning.

19:43.056 --> 19:45.475
I know. If communication
between the Media Office

19:45.559 --> 19:47.769
and the reporters was going
smoothly in the first place,

19:47.853 --> 19:50.314
our forecast team wouldn't have
to get involved in this at all.

19:50.397 --> 19:52.482
How can you say that
when you hold things back, huh?

19:53.066 --> 19:55.569
Who said that you could
keep on crossing boundaries?

19:55.652 --> 19:58.238
You should know since you've been
at Headquarters for so long.

19:58.322 --> 20:00.449
Our forecast room is the KMA's heart.

20:01.533 --> 20:04.411
Do you know a heart that would ask
for your permission to beat?

20:05.078 --> 20:06.205
What?

20:09.082 --> 20:11.668
If you really wanna stay enlightened
regarding our forecasts,

20:11.752 --> 20:13.003
come to the Situation Room,

20:13.086 --> 20:15.380
and you can watch
the way we handle things.

20:55.879 --> 20:57.214
Who does he think he is?

20:57.798 --> 21:00.550
I mean, am I wrong to ask
for an immediate update

21:00.634 --> 21:03.136
for the Spokesperson's Office
on the severe weather conditions?

21:03.220 --> 21:06.306
Also, why does he think
he can talk in secret with a reporter?

21:06.390 --> 21:07.975
A reporter who's married too.

21:08.058 --> 21:09.434
The nerve of that punk.

21:10.394 --> 21:11.979
She's my wife.

21:13.188 --> 21:16.900
And worse, they were talking right here
on KMA grounds for everyone to see?

21:16.984 --> 21:17.901
You found out.

21:19.111 --> 21:19.987
What?

21:20.779 --> 21:23.031
Lee Si-woo is Chae Yu-jin's ex.

21:24.866 --> 21:27.452
- You knew about it?
- Mm-hmm.

21:27.536 --> 21:29.663
- For how long?
- Since he first came here.

21:31.415 --> 21:33.750
And you still let him on
to your team?

21:33.834 --> 21:36.545
Hey, Director, don't you think
that's inappropriate?

21:36.628 --> 21:39.131
You knew it was inappropriate
to go out with Chae Yu-jin, and yet…

21:39.214 --> 21:40.215
Hey, now, that's…

21:41.717 --> 21:43.510
Wow.

21:44.845 --> 21:47.347
You're pretty scary now, huh?
I gotta watch out.

21:48.390 --> 21:49.308
So what?

21:49.391 --> 21:52.144
You want to see
how I'd react if I saw him around?

21:52.227 --> 21:54.271
Is that what you wanted, revenge?

21:54.354 --> 21:55.522
What?

21:56.565 --> 21:58.734
I guess you're willing
to do anything to torment me.

21:58.817 --> 22:01.278
You thought I was weak, huh?
Well, I'm not.

22:01.862 --> 22:05.365
I'm not gonna let something small
like this get under my skin, okay?

22:06.366 --> 22:08.410
- Han Ki-jun, stop imagining things--
- Wait a minute.

22:10.370 --> 22:11.288
Are you…

22:13.623 --> 22:15.667
still heartbroken over us?

22:17.919 --> 22:20.213
Hey, Ha-kyung, come on here.

22:20.797 --> 22:22.799
Okay. So you moved him
to Headquarters? What now?

22:23.717 --> 22:25.218
I married her.

22:25.302 --> 22:27.304
You can't make me come back to you--

22:27.387 --> 22:29.431
Ah!

22:31.391 --> 22:34.644
I already had enough on my plate
this morning, now this bullshit.

22:34.728 --> 22:37.814
Hey, call me outside like this
one more time, and I'll…

22:37.898 --> 22:40.359
If it happens again,
I'll file a report against you,

22:40.442 --> 22:41.651
and you'll be reprimanded.

22:41.735 --> 22:43.779
Okay, Deputy Director?

22:51.453 --> 22:52.829
Yeah, I was right.

22:53.622 --> 22:55.457
Still heartbroken over us.

22:59.294 --> 23:01.922
SAFE COUNTRY, PEACEFUL PEOPLE

23:20.774 --> 23:21.775
I pulled all the…

23:21.858 --> 23:24.069
all the flash floods
that caused a lot of damage.

23:24.152 --> 23:25.278
Okay. Put it down.

23:26.238 --> 23:27.239
Over here?

23:29.074 --> 23:30.075
Uh…

23:32.494 --> 23:34.204
Do you want anything to drink right now?

23:34.955 --> 23:35.789
No, I'm okay.

23:38.333 --> 23:39.918
Listen, are you upset with me?

23:45.173 --> 23:46.174
What are you saying?

23:46.758 --> 23:47.801
It seems like you are.

23:48.385 --> 23:52.055
Is it because I disagreed with you
in front of the Director General?

23:52.764 --> 23:54.266
Did that irritate you?

23:55.267 --> 23:57.144
Listen, Forecaster.

24:07.863 --> 24:08.697
Come on.

24:20.542 --> 24:23.462
Why did he have to show off
in front of the Director General?

24:24.421 --> 24:25.964
Now we're all suffering,

24:26.047 --> 24:27.924
- because he made Director Jin angry--
- Stop.

24:28.008 --> 24:30.093
Go analyze if you have time to complain.

24:30.927 --> 24:31.887
Hmm.

24:47.152 --> 24:48.737
Forecaster, you--

24:55.035 --> 24:56.077
What are you doing?

24:56.661 --> 24:58.455
Don't worry. We're alone.

24:59.414 --> 25:00.832
Is this why you provoked me?

25:02.042 --> 25:03.210
I didn't know such thing.

25:03.877 --> 25:06.129
I asked because I was really worried.

25:07.756 --> 25:10.884
While we're at work, stay at least
one meter away from me. Clear?

25:16.973 --> 25:19.476
So, uh, what did you
and Ki-jun talk about?

25:21.603 --> 25:24.439
I just wanted to know why that guy
would have, uh, wanted

25:24.523 --> 25:26.483
to, uh, talk to you outside.

25:29.528 --> 25:31.488
I didn't ask you,
so why are you asking me?

25:35.867 --> 25:38.578
I didn't ask you why Chae Yu-jin
was calling you in the morning.

25:38.662 --> 25:39.996
So why would you ask me?

25:42.249 --> 25:44.584
Is that why you were so cold over?

25:45.710 --> 25:46.920
Well, I didn't say that.

25:48.630 --> 25:50.924
- It's true, though, isn't it?
- One meter.

25:52.592 --> 25:54.052
- That was why--
- One meter.

25:56.221 --> 25:59.474
I guess Han Ki-jun found out
I used to go out with her.

25:59.558 --> 26:01.851
It seemed like he was giving Yu-jin
a hard time.

26:01.935 --> 26:05.897
She asked me to be more careful,
so I said I would. That's it.

26:07.524 --> 26:09.985
I understand.
Ki-jun does like to hold a grudge.

26:11.278 --> 26:14.364
And it's your turn to tell me
what Han Ki-jun wanted.

26:17.325 --> 26:22.455
He asked, uh, if I was trying to hurt him
by adding you to my team.

26:22.539 --> 26:26.334
If it was on purpose or what
because you're his wife's ex-boyfriend.

26:26.418 --> 26:28.044
Why would I want revenge?

26:28.128 --> 26:31.131
Also, we wouldn't have started
all this madness

26:31.214 --> 26:32.757
just to get revenge on anyone.

26:32.841 --> 26:33.758
Am I right?

26:33.842 --> 26:36.845
"Madness"? Really?

26:36.928 --> 26:40.390
I just suffered through so much
for dating a coworker, now here we are.

26:40.473 --> 26:42.726
So, yeah. Madness sounds right.

26:46.479 --> 26:47.897
You make a good point.

26:53.069 --> 26:56.615
I'm just mad I didn't catch
the cold air coming from the north.

26:58.450 --> 26:59.492
Yeah, I know.

27:01.786 --> 27:03.288
Okay, then. See you.

27:04.914 --> 27:06.458
Can I come to your place after work?

27:08.251 --> 27:09.753
If you bring a bottle of Pinot Noir.

27:09.836 --> 27:10.962
Done!

27:16.926 --> 27:19.304
Stop messing around. Okay, Forecaster?

27:19.929 --> 27:20.889
Yes, ma'am.

27:32.484 --> 27:34.235
She's so annoyed with me right now.

27:34.986 --> 27:36.613
She's actually really harsh.

27:37.280 --> 27:38.865
You wouldn't think so, and well…

27:38.948 --> 27:41.034
Mm. Yeah, no one asked.

27:43.411 --> 27:44.621
'Kay.

28:11.606 --> 28:13.858
We have a washing machine, you know.

28:17.612 --> 28:19.197
Have you heard from Ha-kyung yet?

28:21.116 --> 28:24.577
Mom, these days, people even
wanna have a dog choose its own life.

28:24.661 --> 28:27.038
So it's not at all cool for a mother

28:27.122 --> 28:29.416
to submit all
of her daughter's information

28:29.499 --> 28:32.961
to a matchmaking plan
and not even ever go and ask her.

28:34.462 --> 28:36.047
I didn't do it for me.

28:36.131 --> 28:38.758
If she marries a guy
that's actually worth her time,

28:38.842 --> 28:42.971
her life will be simple, and I'd be
so proud to tell everyone about it.

28:43.888 --> 28:45.765
I sacrificed so much raising her.

28:45.849 --> 28:48.017
So can't I have
this one thing as a parent?

28:48.101 --> 28:50.937
That's more for you than for Ha-kyung.

28:51.020 --> 28:52.355
Ah, shut it.

28:52.439 --> 28:53.732
Go in.

28:53.815 --> 28:56.901
Do some work. Don't leave
your deadline to the last second.

29:09.831 --> 29:11.166
Should I call her?

29:13.084 --> 29:15.962
Just forget it. I'm a woman with pride.

29:21.384 --> 29:23.970
You can have it, Mom.

29:40.820 --> 29:42.030
What's wrong, huh?

29:43.031 --> 29:44.115
Nothing.

29:44.199 --> 29:45.658
Did you have a fight with your husband?

29:46.534 --> 29:47.452
No, we didn't fight.

29:48.036 --> 29:49.537
What's it about? In-laws?

29:49.621 --> 29:51.956
Different lifestyles?
Or does he want to have a child?

29:52.040 --> 29:53.124
Nothing like that.

29:55.794 --> 29:57.962
Oh, hi. Mind if I join my wife?

29:58.046 --> 30:00.048
Oh, hello, Deputy Director.

30:00.131 --> 30:01.299
Please eat.

30:03.468 --> 30:05.094
Why, uh, why just soup, huh?

30:05.178 --> 30:06.513
The bulgogi looked good today.

30:08.264 --> 30:09.265
Here, try.

30:15.396 --> 30:18.608
Yu-jin will always go for a great steak.

30:19.192 --> 30:21.236
And she never even ever gains a pound.

30:21.319 --> 30:23.321
Some people just have
really amazing genetics, huh?

30:23.404 --> 30:26.074
Oh, yeah. Right.

30:31.371 --> 30:32.747
Give me a minute, okay?

30:37.293 --> 30:38.419
What are you doing?

30:39.796 --> 30:41.673
I'm helping you save your reputation.

30:42.465 --> 30:44.092
Why? Should I not?

30:44.175 --> 30:46.177
Do you want me to show up
and keep arguing instead?

30:46.261 --> 30:47.595
"Arguing"?

30:48.221 --> 30:49.305
You were the one who--

30:49.389 --> 30:50.890
Huh, what were you saying to her?

30:53.476 --> 30:54.602
Oh, hello.

30:57.939 --> 31:00.316
That jerk was so cocky earlier.

31:00.400 --> 31:02.610
He didn't even seem sorry or guilty.

31:02.694 --> 31:04.571
Why would he be sorry or guilty?

31:04.654 --> 31:05.822
We're not together.

31:06.865 --> 31:09.117
Are you really taking that bastard's side?

31:09.200 --> 31:10.493
It's not like that.

31:10.994 --> 31:13.705
Regardless, I don't even want you
seeing him by accident anymore.

31:13.788 --> 31:16.833
And if you do run into him,
don't even say hi.

31:16.916 --> 31:18.418
Don't look at him, get it?

31:18.501 --> 31:20.628
Well, how about you just ask me to quit?

31:22.255 --> 31:23.506
- Would you?
- Oppa.

31:23.590 --> 31:25.925
There's ton of other places
for a reporter to work,

31:26.009 --> 31:27.927
like police stations
or the Prosecutors' Office.

31:28.011 --> 31:30.597
Why don't you move to another office
if you're so uncomfortable?

31:30.680 --> 31:31.931
Hey, hey.

31:32.015 --> 31:34.601
My job here is perfect.
You know I can't go.

31:35.310 --> 31:36.519
And listen to me, Yu-jin.

31:36.603 --> 31:39.272
You better stop talking back
to me like that.

31:39.856 --> 31:42.317
I'm only letting it slide
because I'm so nice.

31:42.400 --> 31:44.277
Hard to imagine you if you weren't.

31:44.903 --> 31:48.698
Anyway, I really hope
you won't lie to me ever again, okay?

31:49.282 --> 31:52.493
Gosh, I'm sorry.
My family just called.

31:52.577 --> 31:54.329
Eat your soup. It's getting cold.

31:55.371 --> 31:56.414
You too, babe.

32:08.176 --> 32:09.052
Mm.

32:12.347 --> 32:13.306
Eat it all up.

32:14.641 --> 32:16.309
You're making me blush

32:16.392 --> 32:17.685
in front of Reporter Cho.

32:17.769 --> 32:20.313
See? Yu-jin cares about me so much.

32:21.940 --> 32:22.857
Ooh.

32:24.317 --> 32:26.027
Mm, delicious.

32:26.110 --> 32:27.070
Mm.

32:41.000 --> 32:43.086
- One Americano, please.
- Of course.

32:44.003 --> 32:47.882
I heard Director Jin lost it
because some new guy stood up to her.

32:49.133 --> 32:51.761
Well, it wasn't that bad, though.

32:51.844 --> 32:53.304
I heard Ms. Kim Soo-jin

32:53.388 --> 32:56.265
from your team complaining
and pouting about it.

32:56.349 --> 32:59.185
She said that
Director General scolded Director Jin

32:59.268 --> 33:02.355
and she got so mad, she made the team
analyze ten years' worth of data.

33:02.438 --> 33:05.733
I just think it's wrong to take it out
on your subordinates like that, you know?

33:05.817 --> 33:07.443
You must be having a hard time.

33:08.403 --> 33:10.446
It was nice
when Director Choi was around.

33:10.530 --> 33:11.698
Well…

33:11.781 --> 33:13.825
I'm sure she'll figure things out soon.

33:14.409 --> 33:15.660
Here's your Americano.

33:16.786 --> 33:19.414
She does scare me a little
every time I see her.

33:19.497 --> 33:21.207
'Cause she seems so cold.

33:21.290 --> 33:23.626
- I know.
- It's not fair.

34:03.416 --> 34:04.459
Director Jin.

34:06.502 --> 34:07.670
Gone to lunch yet?

34:09.922 --> 34:11.632
Oh, I'm coming back from it.

34:11.716 --> 34:13.760
We had kalguksu
at the place up the street.

34:13.843 --> 34:16.095
Mm, sounds good.

34:17.930 --> 34:20.516
Oh, uh, didn't you say you were staying

34:20.600 --> 34:21.893
- at the training center, Si-woo?
- Yeah.

34:21.976 --> 34:24.520
Then how did you run
into Director Jin this morning?

34:26.481 --> 34:28.191
The training center is right over there.

34:33.738 --> 34:34.697
Uh…

34:35.698 --> 34:36.908
Uh…

34:41.370 --> 34:43.414
Yes, this is Kim Soo-jin
from Chief Team Two.

34:43.498 --> 34:45.792
I'm calling about the rain echo
in Seoul right now.

34:46.584 --> 34:47.710
E… echo?

34:50.088 --> 34:51.089
Ah, just a moment.

34:52.298 --> 34:54.842
Mr. Um, it's the Metropolitan Office.

34:54.926 --> 34:57.095
They're saying the rain echo
over Seoul looks abnormal.

34:57.178 --> 34:59.097
- Could you please take a look?
- Huh?

34:59.806 --> 35:00.723
What?

35:01.474 --> 35:02.433
Oh!

35:04.811 --> 35:08.731
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

35:09.482 --> 35:11.609
What? But why?

35:14.445 --> 35:17.907
- Tsk, touring a house that early?
- Yeah, an apartment.

35:19.408 --> 35:21.661
I guess the landlord's schedule
was really full,

35:21.744 --> 35:23.663
so they were only available
in the morning, right?

35:23.746 --> 35:24.622
That's, that's right?

35:24.705 --> 35:26.290
Oh, yeah, that's the story.

35:26.374 --> 35:29.335
It was all the landlord's schedule. Yeah.

35:32.797 --> 35:35.550
You sure know a lot about the tour,
considering you weren't there.

35:39.595 --> 35:42.140
I know.

36:11.544 --> 36:14.380
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

36:15.631 --> 36:16.883
Let's hurry home.

36:17.633 --> 36:19.135
Mom, I'm getting wet!

36:23.931 --> 36:25.016
It's raining.

36:27.852 --> 36:28.978
What should we do?

36:35.067 --> 36:37.904
Let's go!

36:37.987 --> 36:39.488
Come on! Hurry!

36:52.752 --> 36:55.087
Mom, did the weather forecast
say that it would rain?

36:55.171 --> 36:56.172
Oh, no!

36:56.255 --> 36:57.840
Goodness!

36:57.924 --> 36:59.342
They didn't say anything.

37:00.718 --> 37:02.970
Do you think I would
have hung the laundry out for this?

37:03.054 --> 37:04.388
Oh.

37:05.723 --> 37:07.141
- Gosh. Darn it.
- Oh, no.

37:08.100 --> 37:10.061
It's like all hell's breaking loose.

37:16.400 --> 37:19.362
Hey, KMA! What do you guys
even do over there, huh?

37:19.445 --> 37:21.781
Why didn't you say anything
about this sudden rainstorm?

37:21.864 --> 37:25.159
This is why they say you guys
are never right about anything! Jesus!

37:29.580 --> 37:32.875
AUTOMATIC CONTROL PANEL

37:47.139 --> 37:48.182
Huh?

37:48.266 --> 37:49.850
- What's going on?
- The lights are out.

37:49.934 --> 37:52.895
- Oh, my God.
- Huh? What's happening?

37:53.562 --> 37:55.314
Is it our problem or the city?

37:55.398 --> 37:58.317
- We should go check the fuse.
- Hey, get some more…

37:58.401 --> 38:01.529
I don't care! The entire building
has no power right now!

38:01.612 --> 38:04.407
What are you going to do? You know
how much this is gonna cost us, huh?

38:04.949 --> 38:07.660
I think you should find a new line of work
if you can't even forecast rain.

38:07.743 --> 38:08.828
You're wasting all our won.

38:08.911 --> 38:11.831
Are you going to compensate us for all
the business we're losing right now?

38:14.333 --> 38:15.960
Why weren't you monitoring the live data?

38:17.003 --> 38:18.212
I was.

38:18.296 --> 38:19.463
And then…

38:21.507 --> 38:22.550
I missed it.

38:24.760 --> 38:26.387
Why? What were you doing?

38:29.265 --> 38:32.143
Is there something up with you?
Are you doing this purposely?

38:32.226 --> 38:34.395
Director, I think
that's too much, you know.

38:34.478 --> 38:37.690
A forecaster ignoring live data
is dereliction of duties.

38:37.773 --> 38:40.735
If the damage is severe enough,
you could be let go from your station.

38:42.528 --> 38:44.363
Even if we saw the rain echo,

38:44.447 --> 38:47.116
there only would have been
a few minutes before it started.

38:47.199 --> 38:48.701
The flooding couldn't have been
prevented regardless.

38:48.784 --> 38:50.369
The damage would have been less serious.

38:50.453 --> 38:52.538
How? It'd still rain 80mm per hour.

38:52.621 --> 38:53.831
That's enough.

38:53.914 --> 38:55.082
I'm sorry.

38:55.166 --> 38:56.959
It's my fault, okay? Stop it.

39:02.423 --> 39:03.507
I'm sorry.

39:04.717 --> 39:07.636
I missed the rainstorm
'cause I was going through old reports.

39:09.555 --> 39:10.931
So what are you saying?

39:13.434 --> 39:18.564
Truthfully, isn't it impossible to analyze
ten years of data in one afternoon?

39:19.148 --> 39:21.442
If I had been more focused
on real-time monitoring--

39:21.525 --> 39:23.569
You're very confused, Ms. Kim Soo-jin.

39:25.738 --> 39:30.076
Analysis and real-time reports
are equally important duties here.

39:30.159 --> 39:32.495
Claiming you missed one
because of the other

39:32.578 --> 39:35.081
is lazy and a poor excuse. Got it?

39:39.085 --> 39:41.045
But it's not an excuse.

39:42.797 --> 39:44.673
I really tried my best, you know, just--

39:45.883 --> 39:46.967
Um, Ms. Kim…

39:47.051 --> 39:50.346
I'm sorry. I'm sorry
I'm not capable enough for you.

39:51.806 --> 39:56.477
Still, I was trying hard, okay?
So please stop implying that I wasn't.

40:03.901 --> 40:05.694
What a great department we are.

40:20.835 --> 40:22.753
Director Jin and Senior Forecaster Um.

40:23.462 --> 40:25.214
The Director General wants to see you.

40:26.132 --> 40:27.133
Okay.

40:33.139 --> 40:35.724
"As the stream swelled,
the roads were flooded,

40:35.808 --> 40:38.060
12 houses were submerged in water,

40:38.144 --> 40:41.147
and electricity was lost
in an underground mall in Gangnam.

40:41.730 --> 40:44.400
We'll have to wait and see
the full extent of the damage."

40:45.943 --> 40:46.819
Casualties?

40:48.112 --> 40:48.988
Well…

40:50.114 --> 40:51.031
Are there any?

40:51.115 --> 40:54.201
Two workers went missing
during a routine inspection

40:55.661 --> 40:58.122
of a drainage plant at Anreung.

41:01.459 --> 41:03.294
And is the rescue search ongoing?

41:03.377 --> 41:06.714
Emergency services
and facility management have started.

41:07.715 --> 41:09.758
But they haven't reported
any findings yet.

41:09.842 --> 41:11.177
This is a nightmare.

41:12.470 --> 41:13.554
I'm sorry, sir.

41:14.930 --> 41:16.098
It was me.

41:17.141 --> 41:18.184
I missed the signal.

41:19.101 --> 41:22.229
I'll take full responsibility.

41:34.450 --> 41:36.702
Why are you doing
this whole brooding song and dance?

41:36.785 --> 41:37.620
What?

41:37.703 --> 41:40.247
In front of our department
and now in front of our Director.

41:40.331 --> 41:42.750
Why are you so set
on claiming responsibility?

41:42.833 --> 41:45.169
'Cause I didn't notice the signals.

41:45.252 --> 41:47.213
But why? Why would you, though?

41:47.296 --> 41:49.215
You're supposed to be
the great Um Dong-han.

41:49.298 --> 41:52.092
I heard you could spot a rainstorm
from the scent of the east wind.

41:52.176 --> 41:54.845
My impression is you wouldn't notice
if it rained in here.

41:59.099 --> 41:59.934
What?

42:00.726 --> 42:02.978
Does it bother you that
I'm your superior when I'm newer?

42:03.062 --> 42:05.606
No. It's nothing like that.
I already told you--

42:05.689 --> 42:06.732
Just wait!

42:07.399 --> 42:09.485
Since I'm the director of Team Two,

42:09.568 --> 42:12.196
I'm the one who takes responsibility
for this crisis,

42:12.279 --> 42:14.615
and I don't want you saying
that it will be you.

42:16.075 --> 42:17.201
You're out of line here.

42:37.304 --> 42:39.848
People think weather
and climate are the same,

42:39.932 --> 42:41.350
but they are quite different.

42:46.105 --> 42:49.066
While weather changes
from day to day like your feelings,

42:49.149 --> 42:53.404
climate stays consistent through time,
like someone's innate personality.

42:56.365 --> 42:58.826
How can you adapt
to someone's feelings in the moment

42:58.909 --> 43:00.911
when you don't know their personality?

43:06.417 --> 43:08.502
Are you taking
Director Jin's side?

43:08.586 --> 43:09.712
Ah, no.

43:10.421 --> 43:12.381
I'm here to tell you I was wrong.

43:14.508 --> 43:18.095
While I was just trying
to predict the weather, well, see,

43:18.178 --> 43:20.806
Director Jin tried to analyze in detail

43:20.889 --> 43:25.853
how the infinite systems of climate
would actually affect everybody.

43:25.936 --> 43:28.480
Even if the same amount of rain
falls at the same time,

43:28.564 --> 43:31.275
the impact varies from region to region.

43:32.693 --> 43:36.905
When it rains 80mm per hour everywhere,
Yeoksam will be just fine,

43:36.989 --> 43:40.909
but Gangnam will be flooded
because, well, the ground there is lower.

43:42.661 --> 43:46.081
A forecast should reflect that as well.

43:46.165 --> 43:50.294
So it's important to analyze
all the data we can at all times.

43:54.840 --> 43:57.801
She asked us to analyze
ten years' worth of data

43:57.885 --> 43:59.845
to make consumer-centered forecasts,

44:00.888 --> 44:03.724
not forecasts just for…
for the scientists.

44:03.807 --> 44:06.477
I was too focused
on performance and results.

44:07.144 --> 44:10.606
But Director Jin was thinking
of what the people actually need,

44:11.690 --> 44:12.900
what really counts.

44:17.112 --> 44:19.490
Well, it's really hard.

44:21.158 --> 44:22.117
I know.

44:37.633 --> 44:39.551
How are you feeling
about your team members?

44:40.386 --> 44:41.387
Sorry?

44:42.763 --> 44:45.432
Taking responsibility is important.

44:45.516 --> 44:49.061
But you aren't the only one
who's been working hard.

44:49.561 --> 44:52.272
We're all professionals,
and we're all trying to do right.

44:54.983 --> 44:57.069
All of us take this seriously.

45:00.781 --> 45:04.243
You trust that we'll do our best
on the work that you assign us, don't you?

45:04.326 --> 45:07.413
Honestly, I don't think our team
has much confidence in me right now.

45:08.205 --> 45:10.582
They don't have faith
in my orders or decisions.

45:12.459 --> 45:14.795
It's not your orders
that we don't have faith in.

45:15.462 --> 45:16.463
We don't have faith in you

45:16.547 --> 45:20.968
because you're obviously unsure
about your own orders.

45:24.555 --> 45:25.431
Hmm. Ah!

45:26.598 --> 45:27.641
Here.

45:27.725 --> 45:31.478
I analyzed data related to localized
flash floods over the past ten years.

45:31.979 --> 45:33.981
In addition to the main causes
of heavy showers,

45:34.064 --> 45:37.443
I also included cases related
to convergence and divergence

45:37.526 --> 45:39.069
of upper and lower jet streams.

45:39.153 --> 45:40.028
It's all there.

45:41.947 --> 45:42.990
Uh…

45:43.741 --> 45:46.410
Well, I finished what you wanted,
so I guess I'll head out.

45:46.493 --> 45:48.954
Shouldn't you head out too?

45:53.250 --> 45:54.835
Ah, Mom.

45:54.918 --> 45:56.712
Did the kids get soaked earlier?

45:57.546 --> 45:59.840
I know, right?

46:02.760 --> 46:04.219
Exactly. Oh, yes.

46:05.012 --> 46:07.681
I work at the KMA,
and my kids still get caught in it.

46:31.747 --> 46:33.415
Hey, Yu-jin. It's oppa.

46:34.249 --> 46:36.919
I'm heading out right now. Wait for me.

46:37.419 --> 46:40.130
So what do you feel like
for dinner tonight, huh, doll?

46:40.714 --> 46:42.758
Oh, tteokbokki.

46:43.258 --> 46:45.928
Sure. I'll get anything for you, my baby.

46:48.847 --> 46:50.224
No. No, no, no.

46:59.942 --> 47:01.318
- Okay. See you.
- Goodbye.

47:03.654 --> 47:06.532
- Oh, uh, you're going home now?
- Yeah. You?

47:06.615 --> 47:07.449
I should.

47:08.033 --> 47:09.993
Everyone left already. I'm the last one.

47:19.503 --> 47:24.216
ANREUNG RAINWATER DRAINAGE STATION

47:24.299 --> 47:26.009
EMERGENCY RESCUE CONTROL
ON-SITE COMMAND

47:29.555 --> 47:31.223
THIRD PRESS BRIEFING

47:31.306 --> 47:33.892
ANREUNG DRAINAGE STATION
SEARCH FOR MISSING PEOPLE

47:33.976 --> 47:35.519
MISSING WORKERS: 2 PEOPLE

47:51.285 --> 47:53.495
Do you see anything? Keep looking.

47:53.579 --> 47:54.746
Shine the light here.

47:54.830 --> 47:56.081
Look over there too.

47:56.164 --> 47:57.040
- Okay.
- Over there.

47:57.124 --> 47:58.417
Our time is running out.

47:58.500 --> 48:00.460
We have to check
over there too.

48:01.712 --> 48:03.255
I think they're maybe down there.

48:03.338 --> 48:04.965
Shine the light over there.

48:26.486 --> 48:28.447
DANGER

48:28.530 --> 48:29.656
Why are you here?

48:30.657 --> 48:31.491
Oh.

48:32.075 --> 48:34.119
I couldn't sleep, so I thought I should…

48:35.162 --> 48:36.538
I should at least show up,

48:36.622 --> 48:39.833
so they don't think
I'm completely heartless.

48:41.043 --> 48:43.211
- The workers?
- Not yet.

48:55.057 --> 48:56.266
Thank you.

49:15.452 --> 49:16.703
Oh!

49:16.787 --> 49:19.831
The person you are trying
to reach is not available at this time.

49:20.457 --> 49:21.792
Oh, okay, then.

49:24.586 --> 49:26.588
What would she want, huh?

50:07.170 --> 50:09.631
RESTRICTED
KEEP OUT

50:10.924 --> 50:13.135
We found them! Over there!

50:13.218 --> 50:15.762
They're alive! They're fine!
They're over here!

50:17.514 --> 50:19.307
Please let it down carefully.

50:20.058 --> 50:22.436
- Are you okay, sir? Are you okay?
- Clear! Clear!

50:22.519 --> 50:24.479
- Pull the lines. Bring them up.
- Are you okay?

50:26.189 --> 50:28.734
Right there,
right there, be careful, huh.

50:29.568 --> 50:32.154
- Guys, let's bring him in.
- Oh, thank God.

50:32.237 --> 50:34.573
They're okay.

50:35.741 --> 50:37.743
Medic! Get the medic.

50:38.577 --> 50:42.122
- Have you had dinner?
- No. Have you?

50:43.248 --> 50:45.167
Let's go somewhere with a good soup.

50:47.210 --> 50:49.004
Bring them over here!
Over here!

50:50.505 --> 50:52.883
Give us some space. Give us some space.

51:04.269 --> 51:05.103
Oh!

51:06.229 --> 51:07.481
You're not staying at home?

51:11.151 --> 51:12.486
Oh, yeah.

51:13.445 --> 51:14.404
It's a long story.

51:22.788 --> 51:24.790
Door is opening.

51:28.210 --> 51:30.212
Oh, hold on a second.

51:30.295 --> 51:31.421
Thank you.

51:33.215 --> 51:35.717
- Which floor?
- Oh, 12th.

51:36.802 --> 51:38.136
Door is closing.

51:50.440 --> 51:52.192
You live right over us.

51:52.275 --> 51:55.028
1302 or is it 1301?

51:56.238 --> 51:57.614
It's 1302.

51:58.198 --> 51:59.074
Ah.

52:02.410 --> 52:04.830
Well, then, we're neighbors, aren't we?

52:05.330 --> 52:07.374
My sister lives in 1201.

52:10.210 --> 52:12.629
Twelfth floor.
Door is opening.

52:12.712 --> 52:14.047
Have a good night.

52:17.676 --> 52:19.052
Door is closing.

52:27.144 --> 52:28.728
Hmm? Hmm.

52:41.783 --> 52:42.951
Oh, what?

52:43.493 --> 52:44.494
Oh, no.

53:38.048 --> 53:39.925
What is it now?

53:43.845 --> 53:44.846
Uh…

53:53.980 --> 53:55.398
Oh, hello again.

53:55.482 --> 53:57.067
Uh, what can I do for you?

53:57.150 --> 54:00.862
I mentioned earlier
that my sister lives downstairs.

54:00.946 --> 54:02.197
And so?

54:02.280 --> 54:04.115
Well…

54:04.866 --> 54:08.036
- Take these, then?
- What… what for?

54:08.119 --> 54:10.205
Could you please hold on to these
until she comes home?

54:10.288 --> 54:13.458
It's just she's not picking up her phone,
and her door code's changed.

54:13.541 --> 54:15.418
Uh…

54:16.002 --> 54:17.504
Oh, you could ask security.

54:18.255 --> 54:19.297
Oh, I know.

54:19.381 --> 54:22.300
I've already been to their office,
but they're on patrol.

54:23.885 --> 54:28.431
This is all fresh kimchi and bulgogi
our dear mother made for her daughter.

54:29.224 --> 54:31.142
I wouldn't want it all to go bad.

54:31.226 --> 54:33.603
And I can't just carry it all back home.

54:36.147 --> 54:38.066
Please just do me a favor.

54:40.235 --> 54:41.361
Friendly neighbor.

54:41.444 --> 54:43.655
Uh…

54:47.784 --> 54:50.537
I told you. You can wait
for your husband and leave together.

54:50.620 --> 54:52.622
He's having dinner at work,
so he'll be late.

54:52.706 --> 54:55.083
- Is that so?
- Thank you so much for your help today.

54:55.166 --> 54:56.543
Of course. It's my pleasure.

54:56.626 --> 54:58.503
- Good night.
- Good night, Grandma.

54:58.586 --> 54:59.879
Oh. All right.

54:59.963 --> 55:01.715
- Good boy. Let's go now.
- My baby.

55:01.798 --> 55:03.091
- Good night.
- Goodbye.

55:03.174 --> 55:06.177
- Let's go.
- I'm not far if you need something.

55:06.261 --> 55:09.306
- Yeah.
- Okay, get home safely.

55:09.931 --> 55:11.349
Oh, you're so tired.

55:13.226 --> 55:14.561
Oh, Papa!

55:15.895 --> 55:16.771
Huh?

55:17.439 --> 55:19.232
So why are you here, honey?

55:19.316 --> 55:21.234
You were having dinner with friends.

55:22.235 --> 55:23.903
I didn't go.

55:24.946 --> 55:25.864
Why not?

55:27.907 --> 55:29.951
I had a lot of stuff
I wanted to think about.

55:32.162 --> 55:33.663
What's bothering you?

55:35.415 --> 55:36.583
What are you thinking?

55:38.752 --> 55:39.669
Honey.

55:41.212 --> 55:44.674
I wanna take the Level Five
technical exam again.

55:45.467 --> 55:46.384
Hmm?

55:47.844 --> 55:49.721
What will you do about your job?

55:53.475 --> 55:55.518
I'm considering taking a year off.

55:55.602 --> 55:56.728
What do you think?

55:59.981 --> 56:01.900
Hmm.

56:03.318 --> 56:05.028
Ah, no way. No.

56:06.071 --> 56:09.449
Some people may say
that it's okay to make a mistake,

56:09.532 --> 56:12.660
but in our profession,
we cannot tolerate an error.

56:12.744 --> 56:13.745
You're, you're right.

56:14.537 --> 56:17.040
But we shouldn't have
to take total responsibility either.

56:18.166 --> 56:21.669
Predicting and forecasting,
that's our job.

56:21.753 --> 56:25.924
And all the uncertainty
that goes with it, that's also our job.

56:26.883 --> 56:31.262
But assuming responsibility
for every bad thing that happens at all?

56:31.346 --> 56:33.306
It's absurdity.

56:34.682 --> 56:37.936
You were the one who took
responsibility in the first place.

56:38.019 --> 56:40.438
That's 'cause I slipped up, okay?

56:40.522 --> 56:43.608
I'll be responsible
for the mistake I made.

56:43.691 --> 56:45.652
Always.

56:46.236 --> 56:49.531
One little mistake of ours
can kill someone

56:49.614 --> 56:52.534
or cause them to lose
their life savings entirely.

56:52.617 --> 56:56.913
Always stay hyper vigilant
and look for patterns in the weather.

56:57.580 --> 56:59.707
- Know who said that?
- I don't.

56:59.791 --> 57:00.875
Who was it?

57:02.502 --> 57:03.753
Remember what you told me?

57:03.837 --> 57:07.757
You said when you would train
Level Five officers,

57:08.258 --> 57:12.053
"The systems that safeguard whole nations
depend on weather forecasting.

57:12.929 --> 57:15.640
Therefore, a sense of duty
and responsibility

57:15.723 --> 57:17.767
is everything for a forecaster."

57:19.686 --> 57:23.523
If I hadn't taken that class,
I wouldn't be suffering like this now.

57:23.606 --> 57:25.733
I would have been headed straight
to the top, you know.

57:29.404 --> 57:31.281
Did I tell you
to believe in all of that crap?

57:31.865 --> 57:34.951
That was your choice.

57:42.959 --> 57:45.879
So what happened to the man I knew then?

57:47.005 --> 57:48.590
What's gotten into you?

57:51.009 --> 57:53.136
Well, you know.

57:54.971 --> 57:57.056
I think…

57:57.932 --> 58:00.393
I lost some kind of, of drive and…

58:01.060 --> 58:02.061
Hmm?

58:02.729 --> 58:06.065
What's the real reason? What's it all for?

58:06.733 --> 58:10.153
For who really?
A guy needs to answer that.

58:13.990 --> 58:17.368
And now, I don't know how, so, yeah.

58:41.017 --> 58:44.020
Please wait.
Your transaction has been processed.

58:50.860 --> 58:52.987
Please accept your bills.

58:53.071 --> 58:54.405
Thank you very much.

58:57.951 --> 59:01.579
Thank you for using our services.
Please make sure you do not leave…

59:01.663 --> 59:03.915
IMI MOTEL

59:21.849 --> 59:23.393
Oh, careful, careful.

59:24.060 --> 59:26.062
- Oh, easy, easy. You're good.
- Oh.

59:26.145 --> 59:29.857
- Okay. Wait a second, Senior Forecaster.
- Yeah.

59:29.941 --> 59:31.776
Where do you live? What's your address?

59:31.859 --> 59:35.738
Gangwon Province,
Gangneung, Science Complex…

59:35.822 --> 59:38.241
Ah, no, not the Gangwon Office.
Your home in Seoul.

59:38.324 --> 59:41.160
- I'll call a ride for you.
- Huh? "Home"?

59:43.329 --> 59:45.164
Oh, home…

59:46.666 --> 59:48.459
I have no home anymore.

59:49.085 --> 59:53.339
Gang… Gangwon, the KMA… It's the KMA.

59:53.423 --> 59:56.175
I have to go to the KMA.

59:57.802 --> 59:58.928
KMA…

01:00:31.085 --> 01:00:32.211
Mr. Lee?

01:00:36.716 --> 01:00:39.010
Watch the stairs. Oh.

01:00:50.938 --> 01:00:53.024
We have
different personalities,

01:00:53.608 --> 01:00:54.942
different principles,

01:00:55.443 --> 01:00:57.320
and different wounds.

01:00:58.112 --> 01:01:02.617
So it's only natural
for the atmosphere to become unstable

01:01:02.700 --> 01:01:06.412
and an abnormal climate
to appear when we meet.

01:01:06.496 --> 01:01:08.331
Why are you, uh…

01:01:08.831 --> 01:01:10.667
Why are you, uh…

01:01:11.542 --> 01:01:12.794
You're here.

01:01:18.466 --> 01:01:25.473
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

01:01:29.227 --> 01:01:32.730
IMI MOTEL

01:02:11.561 --> 01:02:13.479
I picked up your phone
'cause your sister called.

01:02:13.563 --> 01:02:15.606
She says your mom is really sick.

01:02:15.690 --> 01:02:17.191
They're taking her to the ER right now.

01:02:17.984 --> 01:02:20.528
She'd never listen to the
Assistant Director saying she should.

01:02:20.611 --> 01:02:22.321
I'm all right. Go on back to work.

01:02:24.365 --> 01:02:26.659
I say that
it's time for your investment.

01:02:26.743 --> 01:02:28.661
If you really like my boy…

01:02:28.745 --> 01:02:31.622
Dad, did you say you met with her?

01:02:31.706 --> 01:02:34.083
All last night,
I couldn't stop thinking…

01:02:37.044 --> 01:02:38.379
We should reconsider what we're doing.

01:02:39.130 --> 01:02:40.339
You and me.
